# Civa Android Rules

Before changing code, read:

- `AGENTS.md`
- `docs/PRODUCT_RULES.md`
- `docs/DATA_CONTRACT.md`
- `docs/UI_RULES.md`
- `docs/INTEGRATION_RULES.md`
- `docs/TEST_PLAN.md`

Work only on the assigned Issue and feature branch. Do not change public models,
units, nullability, ownership, navigation, Gradle configuration, or database
schema as an incidental part of another task.

Reuse shared UI and data interfaces. Do not create duplicate models or a second
Android project.

Before proposing a push or pull request, run the real preflight checks and report
their actual results. Never claim an unexecuted check passed and never weaken
tests to make a build succeed.

Stop and report when a contract, authorization rule, transaction boundary, or
schema migration is unclear.
